  "narration": [
    {
      "t": 0.6,
      "text": "The note says how this was sealed. None of it is recorded inside the file, so all of it has to be said again to open it."
    },
    {
      "t": 8.7,
      "text": "Restate the cipher, the stretching and the round count, and it still refuses. Read the error: it names a source file in a provider library and tells you nothing about which of your parameters is wrong."
    },
    {
      "t": 17.4,
      "text": "And it wrote a file anyway, before it noticed. Nonsense, of roughly the right size -- so a check that only looked for the file would have said this worked."
    },
    {
      "t": 28.6,
      "text": "There is one more thing to restate, and it is the one whose default is not what was used. It is on screen."
    },
    {
      "t": 36.8,
      "text": "And it opens."
    }
  ],
  "notes": "A different round count and digest; the task's archive was sealed with other values."
